    "answer": {
      "short": "$-10\\leq x<-3$ or $-3<x\\leq-2$.\n\nMultiply by $(x+3)^2>0$, solve the quadratic inequality and exclude $x=-3$.",
      "worked": "For $x\\ne-3$, $(x+3)^2>0$. Multiply both sides by $(x+3)^2$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2-2&\\geq2(x+3)^2\\\\x^2+12x+20&\\leq0\\\\(x+10)(x+2)&\\leq0\\\\-10\\leq x&\\leq-2\\end{align*}$$\n\nExclude $x=-3$. Thus $-10\\leq x<-3$ or $-3<x\\leq-2$.",
